-- DarkChaos: remove the Cata ore and herb nodes on map 750 and in Deepholm (map 646) (2026-11-14)
--
-- Their yields have no use on 3.3.5: no recipe in Spell.dbc or spell_dbc, no quest, no DC system (item upgrade
-- synthesis, auction-house bot) takes Obsidium/Elementium Ore, Cinderbloom, Stormvine, Azshara's Veil,
-- Heartblossom, their Volatiles, Cata gems or Elementium Geodes. Elementium and Heartblossom also need skill
-- 475-500, which only bots reach (playerbots set skill = level x 5; no real player has Herbalism or Mining).
-- Removed (spawns):
--   map 646   202736  Obsidium Deposit       ore  skill 425  x98
--   map 646   202738  Elementium Vein        ore  skill 475  x98
--   map 646   202739  Rich Obsidium Deposit  ore  skill 450  x98
--   map 646   202741  Rich Elementium Vein   ore  skill 500  x98
--   map 646   202747  Cinderbloom            herb skill 425  x70
--   map 646   202750  Heartblossom           herb skill 475  x217
--   map 750  3802736  Obsidium Deposit       ore  skill 425  x105
--   map 750  3802747  Cinderbloom            herb skill 425  x114
--   map 750  3802748  Stormvine              herb skill 425  x43
--   map 750  3802749  Azshara's Veil         herb skill 425  x14
--   total 955. Kept on purpose: the classic nodes (Copper..Rich Thorium, Peacebloom..Black Lotus) on
--   750/751, whose ores and herbs have working recipes, and every quest herb (Bitterblossom, Flame Blossom, ...).
-- Deepholm's nodes were in 104 spawn pools that hold nothing else (872 pool rows); those go too.
-- Re-running the Deepholm Neltharion spawn layer (30_) or the HyjalCata node import would bring them back.
--
-- Backups first, so the removal can be undone. REPLACE ... SELECT, not DELETE + INSERT: on a re-run the
-- spawns are already gone, so the SELECT finds nothing and the backups stay intact.
-- Re-running the whole file is a no-op. Apply to acore_world, then restart the worldserver.

